bio:

Julia Piaskowski is a consulting statistician for the College of Agriculture at the University of Idaho. She is long-time R user, former SAS user, occasional C programmer, and novice python programmer. She has a B.S. in Molecular Biology, M.S. in Crop Science and PhD in Crop Science. She is passionate about supporting agriculture and agricultural research.
